    "site_desc": "This tower is located on the Edwards Plateau at a site known as the \"Martin Ranch.\" The overall property is approximately 2,000 ha and is owned by Texas A&M. Broadly, vegetation is a mix of woody (~20%) and herbaceous species (including Prosopis, Juniperus, and Quercus and a number of C4 grass and other herbaceous species). Common soils include the Tarrant series (Clayey-skeletal, smectitic, thermic Lithic Calciustolls ). Historic and current land uses include livestock grazing. Future prescribed burning is also planned at the site and may include areas in the footprint of the tower.",
